1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
Most AI coding tools pull the project into the agent.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:17,877
Patchwork flips that model: it lets the Codex session you already have work directly inside the web application, with no embedded chatbot, API key, extension, or separate MCP server.

3
00:00:17,877 --> 00:00:25,600
The human keeps a real local-first workspace: virtual files, a text editor, live preview, checkpoints, and ZIP export.

4
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:32,450
Everything persists in this browser, and the interface still works when Site Tools are unavailable.

5
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:40,863
In ChatGPT's built-in browser, Patchwork registers ten WebMCP tools from the top-level document.

6
00:00:40,863 --> 00:00:49,895
Codex reads the workspace context and only the explicit files it needs. These read operations do not change the revision.

7
00:00:49,895 --> 00:00:57,293
For the transformation, Codex submits one bounded multi-file write with the revision it observed.

8
00:00:57,293 --> 00:01:04,043
Patchwork validates every path and size before changing anything, creates a pre-edit checkpoint,

9
00:01:04,043 --> 00:01:13,763
commits the batch atomically, and increments the revision once. The editor and preview update from that same authoritative workspace.

10
00:01:13,763 --> 00:01:19,540
If any item were invalid, the entire batch would be rejected without a partial write.

11
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:27,573
Codex then inspects the compiler and runtime signals available from the preview.

12
00:01:27,573 --> 00:01:34,900
This run reports no blocking error, so Patchwork makes no invented visual claim.

13
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:40,808
Every mutation remains recoverable through an explicit checkpoint, and project data never goes to a Patchwork backend.

14
00:01:40,808 --> 00:01:48,348
Patchwork makes WebMCP the structured collaboration layer between a real product interface and the agent the user already has.

15
00:01:48,348 --> 00:01:53,293
Try the live demo and inspect the complete open-source implementation.
